second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When did Arthur Middleton die?\", \"slot_hint\": \"death_date\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 63, \"text\": \"to the British in 1780, he was sent as a prisoner of war to St.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00\", \"start\": 64, \"end\": 179, \"text\": \"Augustine, Florida (along with Edward Rutledge and Thomas Heyward Jr.), until exchanged in July the following year.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00\", \"start\": 180, \"end\": 299, \"text\": \"Middleton died on January 1, 1787 at the age of 44 and was buried in the family tomb in the Gardens at Middleton Place.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00\", \"start\": 300, \"end\": 370, \"text\": \"The death notice from the \\\"State Gazette of South-Carolina\\\" (SC), Jan.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00\", \"start\": 371, \"end\": 499, \"text\": \"4, 1787, described him as a \\\"tender husband and parent, humane master, steady unshaken patriot, the gentleman, and the scholar.\\\"\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00\", \"start\": 500, \"end\": 576, \"text\": \"The plantation then passed to Henry, his eldest son, later Governor of South\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 63, \"text\": \"to the British in 1780, he was sent as a prisoner of war to St.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01\", \"start\": 64, \"end\": 179, \"text\": \"Augustine, Florida (along with Edward Rutledge and Thomas Heyward Jr.), until exchanged in July the following year.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01\", \"start\": 180, \"end\": 297, \"text\": \"Middleton died on June 15, 1790 at the age of 47 and was buried in the family tomb in the Gardens at Middleton Place.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01\", \"start\": 298, \"end\": 498, \"text\": \"The death notice from the \\\"State Gazette of South-Carolina\\\" (SC), June 18, 1790, described him as a \\\"tender husband and parent, humane master, steady unshaken patriot, the gentleman, and the scholar.\\\"\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01\", \"start\": 499, \"end\": 585, \"text\": \"The plantation then passed to Henry, his eldest son, later Governor of South Carolina.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 16, \"text\": \"Sarah Middleton.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"start\": 17, \"end\": 121, \"text\": \"Middleton’s father died in 1685, leaving to his wife, Sara, and their young son, Arthur, the plantation.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"start\": 122, \"end\": 289, \"text\": \"In the following decade, English colonists learned how to cultivate rice in fresh water swamps, with slave labor, by 1699, The Oaks plantation had begun to make money.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"start\": 290, \"end\": 376, \"text\": \"By 1720, the estate consisted of over 5,000 acres and Middleton owned over 100 slaves.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"start\": 377, \"end\": 465, \"text\": \"A well-established member of the Carolina gentry, Middleton was also a respected member.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"start\": 466, \"end\": 548, \"text\": \"In 1710, he traveled to London to discuss the political problems in the Carolinas.\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"start\": 549, \"end\": 603, \"text\": \"Middleton died on September 17, 1737 at the age of 56,\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 158, \"text\": \"Arthur Edward Middleton Arthur Edward Middleton (2 November 1891 – 19 October 1953) was a British politician who served as the Chair of London County Council.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03\", \"start\": 159, \"end\": 278, \"text\": \"Middleton qualified as an accountant and served on the council of the Society of Incorporated Accountants and Auditors.\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03\", \"start\": 279, \"end\": 385, \"text\": \"He was a supporter of the Labour Party, and in 1942 was appointed to London County Council as an alderman.\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03\", \"start\": 386, \"end\": 505, \"text\": \"In 1946, he was elected to represent Islington North on the council, and then from 1952 he again served as an alderman.\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03\", \"start\": 506, \"end\": 566, \"text\": \"In addition, he served on the Royal Commission on the Press.\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03\", \"start\": 567, \"end\": 581, \"text\": \"In April 1953,\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Arthur Middleton\", \"scope\": \"Death date\", \"claim\": \"Arthur Middleton died on January 1, 1787.\", \"answer\": \"January 1, 1787\", \"quote\": \"Middleton died on January 1, 1787 at the age of 44 and was buried in the family tomb in the Gardens at Middleton Place.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Arthur Middleton\", \"scope\": \"Death date\", \"claim\": \"Arthur Middleton died on June 15, 1790.\", \"answer\": \"June 15, 1790\", \"quote\": \"Middleton died on June 15, 1790 at the age of 47 and was buried in the family tomb in the Gardens at Middleton Place.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Arthur Middleton\", \"scope\": \"Death date\", \"claim\": \"Middleton died on September 17, 1737 at the age of 56.\", \"answer\": \"September 17, 1737\", \"quote\": \"Middleton died on September 17, 1737 at the age of 56,\", \"original_document_number\": 3}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03:c0\", \"entity\": \"Arthur Edward Middleton\", \"scope\": \"Death date\", \"claim\": \"Arthur Edward Middleton died on 19 October 1953.\", \"answer\": \"19 October 1953\", \"quote\": \"Arthur Edward Middleton Arthur Edward Middleton (2 November 1891 – 19 October 1953) was a British politician who served as the Chair of London County Council.\", \"original_document_number\": 4}], \"R5_answers\": [\"January 1, 1787\", \"June 15, 1790\", \"September 17, 1737\", \"19 October 1953\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"January 1, 1787\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"June 15, 1790\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"September 17, 1737\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"answer\": \"19 October 1953\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
